  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "You can set an avatar to public to make it shareable to everyone. But what about in the cases where you just want to share your personal avatar with a friend? You don't want to make it public, but you do want to share it with a friend or two. A system allowing you to share private avatars to just the people you're okay with using it would be amazing. Especially for like when you're making an avatar. You don't need to create a public of it, or log in with the other persons account to upload it for them as a private when you're trying to give them like the test built of the avatar and get feedback. Instead you can just keep it private, and just share them with like a link or a pedestal in game like you do with emojis and such. What do you guys think? Does this sound like an interesting idea?",
